Supersampling: an antialiasing setting, the samples a pixel (2, 4, 8 or 16; 0 off, the default), raises the render
scale by its square root on top of render_percent, and the present averages the bigger frame over every pixel a
screen pixel covers (Blit's n x n box filter) instead of reading it at one point.

